&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flowdesk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flowdesk, we are building the infrastructure powering the next era of global finance. As a full-service digital asset trading and technology firm, we provide liquidity solutions, OTC trading, and market infrastructure that connect digital assets to global markets with institutional-grade precision, transparency, and scale. Flowdesk combines expertise from traditional finance, algorithmic trading, and blockchain technology to deliver always-on trading capabilities across the digital asset ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, we have grown into a global team supporting institutions, exchanges, and token issuers worldwide as the financial system evolves toward tokenized markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why join Flowdesk? You&#39;ll be joining a company operating at the intersection of finance, technology, and crypto - solving complex market problems, building critical infrastructure, and helping shape how digital assets move globally. We move fast, think long term, and work with a strong ownership mindset across engineering, trading, product, operations, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a key player in the newly formed Core Engineering team at Flowdesk to build a world class back office system which will serve as the backbone for Flowdesks systems. Work alongside a seasoned team with deep product, buy‑side, and sell‑side experience in both Crypto and TradFi.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tasks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeFi Integrations:&lt;/strong&gt; Collect all necessary on-chain data and integrate with decentralized protocols to power an accurate, real-time back office system. You will be responsible for ensuring management has a comprehensive, up-to-date view of all on-chain assets. This includes owning the full process from requirements analysis, task specification, implementation, to post-production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Booking / Aggregation:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement and enhance features in the core booking and aggregation engine (Realised / Unrealised P&amp;amp;L, Balances etc…) ensuring performance, reliability and correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reconciliation:&lt;/strong&gt; Automate reconciliation of all trading and treasury activity across the firm implementing data feeds from internal systems, banking, exchanges and custodians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with the Finance and other internal users to gather and refine requirements, plan milestones, demo progress, and coordinate cutovers from manual / legacy workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data products and APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; Expose well-versioned APIs and event streams for downstream consumers; maintain backward compatibility and schema evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ways of working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow established architecture and coding standards; participate in RFCs/design reviews and propose incremental improvements within existing patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-documented code and meaningful tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to PR reviews; maintain up-to-date technical docs and diagrams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own components end-to-end from spec to production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a problem solver who uses software as a tool to deliver measurable business impact. You enjoy writing and shipping high-quality code, seeing it run in production, and collaborating across teams in a hybrid, cross-location environment. You communicate clearly with stakeholders and care about reliability, security, and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves - Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifecycle knowledge of crypto asset classes: spot, perpetuals, futures, and options (including DeFi implementations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with trade lifecycle including backoffice and post trade&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on integration with Defi protocols (DEX/AMM, lending, derivatives) such as Uniswap v3, Curve, Aave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record delivering scalable, reliable systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable partnering with internal stakeholders across Trading, Ops, Compliance, and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves - Technical:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong OO background in one or more: Go, C++, C#, Java or Rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Typescript and Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API design (versioning, backwards compatibility, observability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postgres schema design and query optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with message queue / pub-sub systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud environments (GCP, AWS, Azure), modern CI/CD and containerization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves - Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or maintained position-keeping / accounting systems (PnL, accounting methods, pricing, greeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Centralized reference data platforms (assets, networks, instruments), consistent symbology and instrument economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trading, risk, or back-office systems, ideally in regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Have - Technical:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rust and/or Solidity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating with nodes/providers. (e.g. QuickNode)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time-series/analytical databases (e.g., ClickHouse, BigQuery)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NATS.io&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;gRPC/Protobuf and high-performance, low-latency services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid, cross-time-zone collaboration with clear documentation and async communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close partnership with platform/infrastructure teams (cloud and runtime) and IT/end-user teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emphasis on secure-by-design, reliable systems and compliance-ready engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flowdesk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flowdesk, we are building the infrastructure powering the next era of global finance. As a full-service digital asset trading and technology firm, we provide liquidity solutions, OTC trading, and market infrastructure that connect digital assets to global markets with institutional-grade precision, transparency, and scale. Flowdesk combines expertise from traditional finance, algorithmic trading, and blockchain technology to deliver always-on trading capabilities across the digital asset ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, we have grown into a global team supporting institutions, exchanges, and token issuers worldwide as the financial system evolves toward tokenized markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why join Flowdesk? You&#39;ll be joining a company operating at the intersection of finance, technology, and crypto - solving complex market problems, building critical infrastructure, and helping shape how digital assets move globally. We move fast, think long term, and work with a strong ownership mindset across engineering, trading, product, operations, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our technology team builds and maintains the low-latency trading infrastructure that powers our operations - from execution engines and exchange connectivity to risk and market data systems. We move fast, operate at scale, and expect our engineers to take direct ownership of production systems that impact live trading P&amp;amp;L.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Rust engineer to join our High-Frequency Trading team. This is a core technical role focused on the components that sit closest to the market: order management, feed handling, and strategy execution. The successful candidate will have direct experience building these systems in production and will be comfortable working at the systems level – networking, parsing, and latency optimisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Order Management System (OMS) development and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed handler design and optimisation - processing market data at high throughput&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy logic implementation and integration with execution infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-level networking code: custom protocol parsing, socket management, kernel bypass techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast parsing pipelines for market data and order flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exchange connectivity across FIX, WebSocket, and proprietary protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Latency profiling, benchmarking, and continuous performance improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct, hands-on experience building OMS, feed handlers, and/or strategy logic in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Rust - the primary language for this role. Experience with both async and non-async (synchronous / bare-metal) Rust is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-level networking: socket programming, protocol implementation, latency-aware design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing fast parsing code - binary protocols, custom formats, minimal-copy pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FIX protocol and WebSocket connectivity in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of distributed systems and state synchronization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TradFi or institutional crypto market-making background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with kernel bypass networking (DPDK, RDMA, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lock-free data structures and wait-free concurrency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Options or derivatives experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C++ background - useful where Rust experience is being built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;London (primary preference)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dubai (also open)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote: considered only for candidates with 1-2+ years at a recognised institutional trading firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Person Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and autonomous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated and results-driven&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong maths and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to successfully manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Culture &amp;amp; Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take Action &amp;amp; Own the Mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be of Service &amp;amp; Contribute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate, Create Value, &amp;amp; Be Courageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act with Integrity &amp;amp; Respect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment (English is the main language)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% health coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team events and offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our process is consistent across all engineering roles and is designed to assess genuine technical depth. Candidates should expect the following stages:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 1:&lt;/strong&gt; First round interview with a member of our Talent Acquisition team (45 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 2:&lt;/strong&gt; Binance take-home assignment, AI-assisted + online technical screen AI-free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 3:&lt;/strong&gt; 30-45 mins with CTO - assessment of system design, technical experience, discussion of AI output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 4:&lt;/strong&gt; Online CoderPad interview with HFT team - Rust focused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 5&lt;/strong&gt;: In-person technical interview covering live-coding, data-structure &amp;amp; algorithms round, and background and goals alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 6: Round-Up meeting with Head of Talent Strategy.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FLOWDESK&amp;nbsp; |&amp;nbsp; www.flowdesk.co&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flowdesk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flowdesk, we are building the infrastructure powering the next era of global finance. As a full-service digital asset trading and technology firm, we provide liquidity solutions, OTC trading, and market infrastructure that connect digital assets to global markets with institutional-grade precision, transparency, and scale. Flowdesk combines expertise from traditional finance, algorithmic trading, and blockchain technology to deliver always-on trading capabilities across the digital asset ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, we have grown into a global team supporting institutions, exchanges, and token issuers worldwide as the financial system evolves toward tokenized markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why join Flowdesk? You’ll be joining a company operating at the intersection of finance, technology, and crypto – solving complex market problems, building critical infrastructure, and helping shape how digital assets move globally. We move fast, think long term, and work with a strong ownership mindset across engineering, trading, product, operations, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identity is the main control point across our SaaS, cloud and internal systems. The Security team makes sure access to sensitive systems is tightly controlled and provable to auditors and regulators, and that the data behind those systems is protected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will plan, build and run our identity provider setup and single sign-on estate, including Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) for all Flowdesk identities. You will also cover Data Protection - data encryption, PKI, Key Management, data classification and DLP from a plan, build and run perspective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work as part of the wider security team, alongside Secure Engineering, IT Operations, HR and application owners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the identity provider and SSO estate: onboarding applications, enforcing MFA, and keeping SAML, OIDC and SCIM integrations healthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run Authentication and Access Management for our own products and internal tools, including OAuth 2.0 flows, token handling and session policy, through Terraform and infrastructure as code where possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and deliver identity projects, such as IdP consolidation, passwordless, conditional access, IGA and JML automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the joiner, mover and leaver process across the organisation, working with IT Operations, HR and application owners so access follows role and is removed promptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement Data Classification, DSPM and DLP capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and manage data protection solutions such as HSMs, Key Management, Secrets and Password Management, and PKI-related solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run privileged access management (PAM) and just-in-time (JIT) access, so elevated access is granted for a set purpose and time, approved, logged and removed automatically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help run regular access review campaigns and manage break-glass accounts and service account governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review application and API authentication designs with Secure Engineering, and advise teams on best practice implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce evidence and reporting for audits and regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor identity logs for abuse, and help respond to account compromise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as part of the wider security team, and cover gaps in other areas when they arise, such as during absences, incidents or peaks in workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years in identity security and data protection, with hands-on delivery of an IdP and SSO rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of SAML, OIDC, OAuth 2.0, SCIM and JWT, including common implementation mistakes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least one enterprise identity provider and one customer or application identity platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PAM and JIT access, ideally for cloud, SaaS and production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the joiner, mover and leaver process, and an understanding of how it works across HR, IT and application teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of Terraform and infrastructure as code, and the ability to work day to day in an environment where infrastructure is managed that way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting skills (required for the role)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General security knowledge across the main domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A process-oriented approach: you document what you do, follow change control, and leave an audit trail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear writing, since much of the job is documenting decisions and explaining them to auditors and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work across the security team and learn adjacent areas, such as incident response, GRC evidence or cloud security, as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly desired&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a regulated, controlled environment, such as financial services or crypto&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Helpful&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer identity (CIAM) experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine identity and secrets management in cloud and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic AI access management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications (CISSP, CISM, CEH or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Person Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented: documents decisions, follows change control and leaves a clear audit trail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator, able to explain technical decisions to both auditors and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across disciplines and stepping in on adjacent security areas when the team needs it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic and automation-minded: prefers infrastructure as code and scripting over manual change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holds a high bar for control and evidence in a regulated, high-trust environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Culture &amp;amp; Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take Action &amp;amp; Own the Mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be of Service &amp;amp; Contribute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate, Create Value, &amp;amp; Be Courageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act with Integrity &amp;amp; Respect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment (English is the main language)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% health coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team events and offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;styles--2Kv6p&quot; data-ui=&quot;careers-page-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flowdesk, we are building the infrastructure powering the next era of global finance. As a full-service digital asset trading and technology firm, we provide liquidity solutions, OTC trading, and market infrastructure that connect digital assets to global markets with institutional-grade precision, transparency, and scale. Flowdesk combines expertise from traditional finance, algorithmic trading, and blockchain technology to deliver always-on trading capabilities across the digital asset ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, we are a global team supporting institutions, exchanges, and token issuers to enable a tokenized financial markets ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why join Flowdesk? You’ll be joining a company operating at the intersection of finance, technology, and crypto; solving complex market problems, building critical infrastructure, and helping shape how digital assets connect to global liquidity. We move fast, think long term, and work with a strong ownership mindset across engineering, trading, product, operations, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this role, we are actively looking for bright, young talent who are enthusiastic about learning and developing their trading skills. This opportunity in a fast-paced environment, where there is a strong emphasis on in-depth research and the generation of alpha. Successful candidates will be immersed in a challenging yet rewarding atmosphere, gaining hands-on experience and contributing to innovative trading strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide first-level support to the trading activities.&lt;br&gt;Develop and improve trading strategies on both centralized (CEX) and decentralized (DEX) exchanges.&lt;br&gt;Generate post-trade analysis reports.&lt;br&gt;Assist traders in their day-to-day crypto operations.&lt;br&gt;Own a 6 month project to deliver at the end of the internship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background and experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Master’s degree in Quantitative Finance, Mathematics, Computer Science, or Statistics.&lt;br&gt;Strong coding skills with proficiency in Python and SQL; Rust experience is a plus.&lt;br&gt;Solid understanding of cryptocurrency concepts, including wallets, blockchains, smart contracts, and stablecoins.&lt;br&gt;Ability to manage multiple tasks effectively in a fast-paced, collaborative environment.&lt;br&gt;Fluent in spoken and written English.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conditions to participate in the Early Talent Program&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Start Date, starting from October 2026&lt;br&gt;What would be the Internship duration? 6 months (5 days in a week, full time, on-site)&lt;br&gt;Who is eligible? Final-year students or recent graduates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;International environment (English is the main language)&lt;br&gt;50% of transportation costs &amp;amp; a sustainable mobility agreement&lt;br&gt;Swile lunch voucher (€9.25 per day, 60% covered)&lt;br&gt;Team events and offsites&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our process is consistent across all roles and is designed to assess genuine technical depth. Candidates should expect the following stages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stage 1: Online technical assessment&lt;br&gt;Stage 2: Onsite interview with the Trading team (60&#39;)&lt;br&gt;Stage 3: Wrap-up interview with TA (30&#39;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the agenda, discussions rather than trick questions! These moments of exchange will allow you to understand how Flowdesk works and its values. But they are also (and above all) an opportunity for you to present your career path and your expectations for your next job!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to an inclusive and accessible recruitment process. If you require any reasonable adjustments or have specific needs to enable you to participate fully in the interview or assessment process (e.g., a sign language interpreter, extra time for a test, or an accessible location), please contact us to discuss how we can support you.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
